# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and personal data. Everything here can open a real door or identify a
# real home, so the patterns are deliberately unanchored: a `lockData.json` in a
# subdirectory is exactly as dangerous as one in the root, and `git add -A` does
# not care which you meant.
#
# `scripts/check-secrets.sh` (run in CI) is the backstop if something slips
# past these patterns.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Real lock credentials (AES key, admin passcode, unlock key).
# Copy sample-lockData.json to lockData.json and fill in your own.
lockData.json
lockdata.json
*lockData*.json
!sample-lockData.json

# Sciener/TTLock app database — contains every paired lock's keys.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Bluetooth packet captures: contain your lock's address and traffic.
*.pklg
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.btsnoop

# Reverse-engineering notes: contain real device addresses and captured frames.
ttlock_conversation_report.md

# Scratch space for diagnostics: capture logs, one-off scripts, decrypted
# frames. Anchored to the root. Everything here names a real device — an
# advertisement log is a list of your lock's MAC and everything it broadcasts —
# and none of it belongs in history.
/tmp/

# Top-level shell scripts are personal scratch (editor wrappers, one-off
# helpers) and are not part of the project. Anchored to the root, so scripts
# that belong to the repo live in scripts/ and stay tracked.
/*.sh

# Top-level logs are capture scratch and name a real device — an advertisement
# log is the lock's MAC repeated once per report. Anchored to the root for the
# same reason as the line above; logs that belong to the project would live
# under docs/ or tmp/.
/*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/target
/result
/result-*

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/

.ruff_cache/
.direnv/
.DS_Store
.env
